<article class="env-lemma" id="0349C1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0349C1">Lemma <span data-tag="0349C1">6.5.3.7</span>.</a> The inclusion $\Nerve (\cDelta ^{op}_{s}) \subseteq \Nerve (\cDelta ^{op})$ is cofinal. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Theorem <a href="/tag/A37F6A" data-tag="A37F6A">4.1.3.1</a>, it will suffice to prove that for every $n \geq 0$, the category $\calC = \cDelta _{s} \times _{\cDelta } \cDelta _{/ [n]}$ has weakly contractible nerve. To prove this, we let $F: \calC \rightarrow \calC $ be the constant functor taking value given by the inclusion $[0] \subseteq [n]$, and $G: \calC \rightarrow \calC $ the functor which carries an arbitrary map $[m] \rightarrow [n]$ to the induced map $[0] \amalg [m] \rightarrow [n]$. We have natural transformations of functors 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  F \rightarrow G \leftarrow \id _{\calC }.  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Let $X$ be the topological space $| \Nerve (\calC ) |$. The natural transformations above show that the identity map $\id _{X}$ is homotopic to a constant, so that $X$ is contractible as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>